# Design: Metal through the host door. The pages spec/core-operations.md and spec/nums.md are the authority; these nodes say what was chosen and why.

n: 5.14.62
name: metal-through-the-door
kind: hub
is: The GPU is reached from Form: a target the processor does not run is a bound blueprint, and what the C header did is a component package over rows of the host.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.1
name: a-target-is-a-bound-blueprint
kind: decision
is: The bootstrap runs no Metal. Under native, a code leaf of a target the processor does not run is run by what its blueprint is bound to, given the leaf and the list of the values. As a binding's implementation such a leaf declines to the recipe beneath, as before. has-target answers for the processor alone, and a target binds the entry to answer for itself.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.60 5.19.37 7.21 5.9.2
conf: mid
why: Run on 2026-11-27 on an M4 Max: the image flow of make check answered the bytes the C dispatch gave for the same five requests, a 65-lane map in both operand orders, the empty vector and two invalid shapes, from a directory holding only the image. The same holds against main's later flow, where an application calls the map inside one search in both operand orders. The bootstrap went from 2,000 lines to 1,909.
flip: A dispatch walked through rows takes about 6.3 ms where the C took 3.5, and a start 46 ms where it took 5, most of it the one question to the device. Where that matters the rows can be emitted as moves and a call, or the device and pipeline kept between maps.
limit: Rows exist for Apple's arm64 convention only, so under Rosetta, where the C dispatch ran, has-target now answers no and a map answers no-native. A library leaf bound as an entry's implementation no longer runs the map. One line of C still names the target, for the collector. One machine.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.2
name: what-a-dispatch-makes-lies-in-a-room
kind: decision
is: The package host/metal.ck runs a map through seven host functions and 28 Objective-C messages, each a row. Every object it makes is noted under its name as it is made, and let go by a row when the dispatch ends, when a fault or a fail leaves it and before the next begins; a note is what no fail undoes. The two sizes of three words go by reference from a room. The package reaches the host only through seven recipes it is handed.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.62.1 5.14.60
conf: mid
why: ground/metal-holds.ck, inside make check-image, holds that a fault raised at the first copy into the buffer comes out as itself with no object held, and that a fail there under an open choice is a fault with no object held. By hand, a fault on the buffer's release left it noted and the next map let it go. The package written as Python by the writer parses.
flip: A host object that must outlive a dispatch, such as a pipeline kept between maps, needs a slot that is not let go at the end.
limit: The shared buffer is the host's memory and is checked against the device's limits only, where the C also compared it with the allowance. What the map takes of the allowance, the output's room and leaf, is taken before any host object is made.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.3
name: the-door-is-opened-ahead
kind: decision
is: A map may run while a choice is open. Everything the host is asked by name is asked when the door is opened with no choice open: each function's address, each message's registered name, the pool's class. A dispatch then makes no call of entry 98: it runs machine code through the berth on addresses it holds, reads its operands where they lie in the region, and lets go of all it made before it answers. Entry 98 stays refused under a choice.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.62.2 5.14.60 5.7.3
conf: mid
why: Main's application calls the map inside an all over two operand orders. With lookups made at each call the reply was the fault irreversible; with the door opened ahead the five replies are the bytes the C dispatch gave. By hand, four maps gathered by one all over two choices answered four vectors.
alt: Holding the map back with after, which cannot give its answer to the search that asked. Refusing, which would end the application's flow.
flip: A dispatch that left something standing in the host, such as a pipeline kept between maps, would have to be made before the choice or be refused under it.
limit: That a dispatch leaves nothing behind is the package's own care and no check of the walker: host.run is not refused under a choice. A buffer's bytes in the host are gone when it is let go, yet what the device did meanwhile is not something a fail could have undone.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.4
name: a-dispatch-leaves-only-its-answer
kind: decision
is: The door runs each dispatch under a choice of its own, notes the answer and fails back, so the frames, links and nodes the walked calls made are given back and a hundredth map leaves in the region what a second leaves. The walker gives back its own as well: a fail carries no answer, a return to a frame gives back the frames a commit left above it, and both trails are empty wherever no choice is open.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.62.3 5.7.3
conf: mid
why: An independent review of the first version measured 268 KB of frames kept per map and a room kept by every check of the allowance. Read from the region after the change: a hundred cuts, host calls and maps in one recursion end with the 5 frames and 2 links they began with, where the maps alone had left 432,965 frames; twelve maps of 4 MB under 128 MB answer, where none of the later ones did. ground/metal-holds.ck holds the equality of fifty maps and twenty-five.
flip: A dispatch that must leave more than an answer, such as a pipeline kept for the next map, notes that as well.
limit: Every map still makes its device and pipeline anew. A map of 65 lanes takes about 6.3 ms where the C took 3.5.
at: 2026-11-27
